# FDD 18 review — "18 - Data Collection & Compliance - Roster of Positions". Ingested per
# abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md against the mied-v3 Staffing graph
# (staffing-domain.ttl / staffing-permissions.ttl / staffing-api.ttl / staffing-sequences.ttl
# / staffing-technical-design.ttl, all loaded together). Per this session's brief, staffing's
# own v1 PositionRosterAggregate (hasEntity staff:Position, staff:Spot) was checked first and
# is indeed the direct match for nearly this entire FDD — this is one of the best-covered FDDs
# reviewed in this project to date.
#
# Source: "18 - Collection & Compliance - Position Roster.docx" + its .md sibling. Read the .md
# first, then unzipped the .docx for comments.xml (10 comments, all short editorial/clarification
# threads between Caswell/Groom/Dontje — retention-schedule wording, a broken hyperlink, "this
# epic is pending workflows with 18.2-18.6", a note that assignment field requirements vary by
# position type (foreshadowing FDD 22 Employee Assignment Details), an open "AI for SOM: need to
# define error message" action item, and a audit-logging-scope clarification (only log completed
# tasks/actions, not page views) that is already reflected in the Addendum's own final wording —
# none surface a live, unresolved contradiction the way FDD 29's cover-letter thread did, so none
# are modeled as standalone Annotations; folded into individual Requirements' sd:notes where they
# bear on a specific story (18.4.1's audit-logging clarification) and otherwise just noted here.
#
# Structure used: a prose "Business Specifications" section + a 38-row "HIGH LEVEL SCENARIOS"
# paraphrase table restate the same content at coarser grain and are SKIPPED per CONVENTIONS.md.
# An "Addendum" with real Feature/story numbering (18.1.1-18.1.9, 18.2.1-18.2.7, 18.3.1-18.3.10,
# 18.4.1-18.4.8, 18.5.1-18.5.9, 18.6.1-18.6.5 — 48 stories total) is the primary Requirement unit
# used below. One genuine Business-Specifications-only feature was never promoted into the
# Addendum's numbering at all — "duplicate/copy an existing position" (its own paragraph, with
# distinct save/delete-before-submission rules) — modeled with a synthetic
# staff:Req_18_BizSpec_DuplicatePosition ID, matching FDD 29's precedent for this exact situation
# (three un-numbered Business-Specifications features there). Total Requirements modeled: 49.
#
# 18.1.5's own title ("Save Validation Errors for Position Creation") does not match its body,
# which is actually the three-step "Add Filled Spot" assignment workflow (Spot Details > Select
# Employee > Confirm and Add) — a leftover/mislabeled heading from an earlier draft, not corrected
# here; sd:title below uses the FDD's literal (mismatched) heading text with a note, sd:statement
# carries the actual (correct) user-story text.
#
# Wireframes: 41 embedded images total (2 in word/media/, captioned but generic/decorative header
# logos, not modeled; 39 in a top-level /media/ folder referenced via the FDD-29-style
# absolute-path relationship-ID quirk, addressed directly to the Addendum's Feature 18.1-18.2
# write-up — no captions). De-duplicated by checksum to 34 distinct images (several are reused
# byte-identical across the doc, e.g. image7=image8=image9). Given the very close 1:1 match
# between this FDD's Addendum stories and staffing's own PositionRoster/Assignment model, 10
# representative images were extracted and viewed to CONFIRM that match rather than to discover
# new structure: the Positions list (staff:Wireframe1), Add New Position form (staff:Wireframe2),
# Position Details page with a Delete option (staff:Wireframe3), all three steps of the "Add
# Filled Spot" workflow (staff:Wireframe4/5/6 — direct visual match for 18.1.5 and for
# staff:Seq_AssignEmployeeToPosition's own three-step shape), the Assignments tab FTE-health
# warning banner (staff:Wireframe7), a two-row Filled Spots table (staff:Wireframe8), the
# "Partially" meets-requirements state with a "See Recommendations" banner (staff:Wireframe9 —
# this is what surfaces the 18.1.7/18.1.8 coverage gap below, since Op_ValidatePlacement's
# responseSchema only has a boolean meetsRequirements, no three-state Yes/Partially/No), and the
# Positions list with its export/download icon circled (staff:Wireframe10 — corroborates the
# 18.3.6/18.5.7 export gap). The remaining ~24 distinct images were not individually viewed;
# spot-checking their filenames/sizes against the ones viewed (several are exact-duplicate reuses
# of the same screens at different points in the Addendum) gives no indication of an undocumented
# additional screen/feature beyond what the 10 viewed images and the Addendum text already cover.
#
# StaffPositionsDetails.xlsx (a companion reference workbook, hyperlinked from the FDD body
# showing the Education-Job-Type/Local-Job-Category/Local-Job-Function relationship, the same
# kind of "confirmed load-bearing exception" as a Role Matrix) was opened via its .md sibling
# extraction — it is a large, flat cross-reference table of valid Job Type/Category/Function
# combinations (hundreds of rows). It confirms, at a data level, that
# staff:EducationJobType/staff:LocalJobCategory/staff:LocalJobFunction (staffing-domain.ttl) are
# the right value objects and that "for each Education Job Type and Local Job Category, the
# Staffing Admin defines the allowable Local Job Functions" (FDD line ~104) is exactly the kind
# of admin-configurable value-list relationship already implicit in those ValueObjects — it does
# not introduce any new entity/requirement not already covered by the Addendum's own stories, so
# no separate Requirement was minted for it; referenced only as a SourceDocument for traceability.
#
# Feature 18.5 (Data Input via API and File Upload) surfaces this FDD's single biggest finding:
# staffing-api.ttl has NO bulk-file-upload or file-based ingestion endpoint anywhere for
# Positions (staff:Op_CreatePosition/Op_UpdatePosition/Op_UpdatePositionStatus are all
# single-record REST calls) — a real, confirmed coverage gap, not a documentation oversight
# (staffing-domain.md's own methods list explicitly promises "Online / Bulk file / API"). See the
# coverage-gap Annotation below.
#
# Feature 18.6 (Email/Communication) is out-of-scope for Staffing on the same basis FDD 29 used
# for its own alerts stories: the FDD's own Dependencies section names "Alerts, Emails and
# Communications (6.0)" as the owner, and comm:CommunicationsContext already subscribes to
# several of staffing's own events (CollectionCertifiedEvent, CollectionOpenedEvent, etc.) —
# consistent, corroborating evidence, not a new gap.

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix staff: <urn:solutiondesign:instance:staffing:> .
@prefix comm:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:communications:> .
@prefix orgs:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:organizations:> .

#################################################################
# Source documents
#################################################################

staff:Fdd18Doc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "fdd" ;
    sd:section "abox-tests/mied-fdds/functional-design-docs/18 - Data Collection & Compliance - Roster of Positions/18 - Collection & Compliance - Position Roster.docx" ;
    sd:notes "Covers the Position Roster epic (18.0). Author Caitlin Groom (CEPI); approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI), both 08/04/2025 per the signoff table — but comments.xml contains entries dated through 2026-03-10, well after that signoff date, meaning the document (specifically its Addendum) continued to be actively revised after nominal approval, same pattern FDD 29 documented." .

staff:StaffPositionsDetailsDoc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "review" ;
    sd:section "abox-tests/mied-fdds/functional-design-docs/18 - Data Collection & Compliance - Roster of Positions/StaffPositionsDetails.xlsx" ;
    sd:notes "Reference workbook (hyperlinked from the FDD body) cross-referencing valid Education Job Type / Local Job Category / Local Job Function combinations. Confirms staff:EducationJobType/staff:LocalJobCategory/staff:LocalJobFunction are the right value objects; introduces no new entity or requirement beyond what the Addendum already covers." ;
    sd:definedIn staff:Fdd18Doc .

